    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42214" root="وقح" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاحُ الذَّنَبِ</span></b>  (assumed tropical:)  A man <i>patient in riding.</i> (IAar,
K.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَنَبٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاحٌ</span> (S, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَاقِحٌ</span></b> 
(K,) A <i>hard</i> solid hoof, (S, K,) and camel's
foot, and the back; the former an epithet both
masc. and fem.: (TA:) pl. of the former
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وُقُحٌ</span>, (S, K,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وُقَّحٌ</span>. (TA.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَرَسٌ وَقَاحٌ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>A
hard and strong horse.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقِحٌ</span>.

